      "leadSummary": "Parabolic diffusion processes in continuum physics: macroscopic conservation of thermal energy and Fourier's law of conduction, weak and strong maximum/minimum principles, uniqueness and stability theorems, Fourier separation of variables under Dirichlet, Neumann, and Robin boundary conditions, Duhamel's principle for inhomogeneous source distributions, and the Gaussian fundamental solution (heat kernel) on infinite domains.",
